<title>THAILAND: Bangkok Bank of Commerce Q3 turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Bangkok Bank of Commerce Q3 turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited financial results for the first nine months ending Septemer 30, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (in millions of baht unless stated)</p>
<p>					 Third quarter</p>
<p>				   1996			1995</p>
<p>    Shr (baht)    loss     0.32    vs  profit    0.27</p>
<p>    Net	     loss   696.92    vs  profit  198.16</p>
<p>					 Nine months</p>
<p>    Shr (baht)    loss     1.20    vs  profit    0.88</p>
<p>    Net	     loss 1,667.82    vs  profit  662.31</p>
<p>NOTE: Bangkok Bank of Commerce was placed under state control in May when it was found to be carrying huge amounts of non-performing loans.</p>
<p>Total authorised share capital in the period amounted to 3.65 billion shares in 1996 vs 1.07 billion the year before. Totoal issued and fully paid-up share capital amounted to 3.55 billion shares in 1996 vs 800 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
